.Dd July 6, 2024
.Dt OO 3cutlet
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm oo
.Nd cutlet object oriented library
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb oo
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ic import Ar oo
.Pp
.Bl -inset -compact
.It Ic def Ar class name \(r?supers? body
.It Ic def Ar super class method *args
.El
.Ss Class Definition
.Bl -inset -compact
.It Ic def property name \(r?name ... ?
.It Ic def class.property name \(r?\(r?=? value ?
.It Ic def method \(r?arguments? body
.It Ic def class\.method \(r?arguments? body
.El
.Ss C++ Imports
.Bl -inset -compact
.It Ft void Fn oo_add_method "cutlet::interpreter &interp" "const std::string &class" "const std::string &method" "cutlet::function_t func"
.It Ft void Fn oo_add_class_method "cutlet::interpreter &interp" "const std::string &class" "const std::string &method" "cutlet::function_t func"
.It Ft cutlet::variable::pointer Fn oo_get_property "cutlet::interpreter &interp" "cutlet::variable::pointer object" "const std::string &name"
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This simple library takes a few cues from smalltalk to add basic
object orientated programming to the cutlet interpreter.
.Pp
The scopes are very basic.
All class and object properties are private and all class and object methods
are public.
When a class is defined, the class is created very much like a function, a
cutlet component.
Therefore class methods are called in the following fashion:
.Ic class_name Ar method_name Ar *args .
.Pp
When a class is created there are two class methods that are automatically
added to the class.
The
.Ic new Ar *args
method which creates a new object variable and calls the
.Ic new
object method if it exists to initialize the object.
The
.Ic type
method which simply returns the string \(aqclass\(aq.
.Pp
Within the class definition object properties are defined with the
.Ic property
keyword and class properties with the
.Ic class.property
keyword.
Multiple object properties can be defined with the
.Ic property
keyword and can be initialized in the
.Ic new Ar *arg
object method.
Only a single class property can be defined with the
.Ic class.property
and the property can be initialize during class creatation.
.Pp
Like properties methods are defined with the
.Ic method
and
.Ic class.method
keywords accordingly.
.Pp
A simple example of a class definition:
.Bd -literal
class my_class {
  property value val2 val3
  class.property count = [m.uint 0]
  class.property a_setting

  method new {name} {
    local value = $name
    local count = [$count + 1]
  }

  method get_value {
    return $value
  }

  class.method get_count {
    return $count
  }
}

global object = [my_class new "My Object"]
.Ed
.Pp
Class and object properties are accessed as if they were local variables.
Variables will resolve as properties first then as a local variable and finally
a global variable.
Using
.Ic local
will set object and class properties values as well.
Properties will be set instead of local variables or arguments so be careful
with variable naming conflicts.
.Pp
The class methods
.Ic type
and
.Ic new
cannot be overridden as they are automatically added to the class.
.Ss Class Inheritance
The
.Nm
library handles multiple inheritance with everything being dynamically
linked, resolved when called.
For example:
.Bd -literal
class my_class {class1 class2} {

  method set {value} {
    ...
    super class1 set $value
    ...
  }

  method action {
    ...
    $self set "Hello"
    ...
  }

  class.method add {value} {
    ...
    super class2 set $value
    ...
  }
}
.Ed
.Pp
Resolving of methods and properties will be done in the order of the classes as
they are listed when the class is defined.
First the current class is searched then the first super class then
the next one and so on.
.Pp
Methods can call super class methods using the
.Ic super
command.
Also methods will have the local variable
.Ar $self
set to the object called to allow the methods to make additional
method calls as needed.
.Sh C++ API
.Bl  -tag -width Ds
.It Ft void Fn oo_add_method "cutlet::interpreter &interp" "const std::string &class" "const std::string &method" "cutlet::function_t func"
Add a native c++ method to a class.
.It Ft void Fn oo_add_class_method "cutlet::interpreter &interp" "const std::string &class" "const std::string &method" "cutlet::function_t func"
Add a native c++ class method to a class.
.It Ft cutlet::variable::pointer Fn oo_get_property "cutlet::interpreter &interp" "cutlet::variable::pointer object" "const std::string &name"
Get a property value from an object.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cutlet 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Ron Wills
.Mt <ron@digitalcombine.ca>
.Sh CAVEATS
.Ic super
is a global function and is not sandboxed to the methods.
It will attempt to check that it is being used within a method and raise an
error if it not.
.Pp
The c++ interface is far from complete.
